From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 23:48:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Own writes into title memory: their write-watch bits are
 reset only while the submission's asking stands

watch::forgot (fork #827) drops the kernel's dirty bits behind a write of ours.
The journal is told of that write by watch::wrote, which does nothing unless a
submission's one asking stands (VICTORY_ASK_ONCE=0, or an asking that found no
watched range). Without it the bits were the only word of the write, and the
host copies of the destination kept the bytes from before. Now the bits are
left set in that case, as before the port.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/victory-gpu/src/host.rs  | 6 +++++-
 crates/victory-gpu/src/watch.rs | 6 ++++++
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/victory-gpu/src/host.rs b/crates/victory-gpu/src/host.rs
index 416391966..cbf740dec 100644
--- a/crates/victory-gpu/src/host.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-gpu/src/host.rs
@@ -6147,7 +6147,11 @@ pub(crate) fn copy_mapped(dst: *mut u8, src: *const u8, len: usize, title_dst: b
         // A title destination the kernel wrote: its pages' dirty bits are
         // the layer's own write. Left set, the next refresh reports them as
         // the title's and copies the same bytes up again, every frame.
-        if title_dst {
+        // Only while the submission's one asking stands: then the caller
+        // tells the journal of this write (`crate::watch::wrote`). With no
+        // asking standing the journal learns of it from these very bits,
+        // and the host copies of the destination would keep the old bytes.
+        if title_dst && crate::watch::asking_stands() {
             crate::watch::forgot(dst as usize, len);
         }
         return;
diff --git a/crates/victory-gpu/src/watch.rs b/crates/victory-gpu/src/watch.rs
index 407982397..efe7afa3e 100644
--- a/crates/victory-gpu/src/watch.rs
+++ b/crates/victory-gpu/src/watch.rs
@@ -232,6 +232,12 @@ pub(crate) fn ask_once_end() {
     }
 }
 
+/// Whether a submission's one asking stands ([`ask_once`]): [`wrote`] then
+/// tells the journal of a write of ours, and does nothing otherwise.
+pub(crate) fn asking_stands() -> bool {
+    JOURNAL.lock().unwrap_or_else(|e| e.into_inner()).kept
+}
+
 /// We wrote title memory `[at, at + len)` while a submission's one asking
 /// stands (the title's buffer copies, done at submission): its pages count
 /// as written after that asking, so the refreshes that follow copy them.
